-- converse.prompt_coherence(prompt): joint orientation + sense resolution.
--
-- NATIVE (src/prompt_coherence.c). The SQL body this replaces hung converse.chat() for
-- every prompt -- >280s measured 2026-07-27 after the UD ingest -- and was taken
-- off the hot path in the same change that ported it. It was SQL doing what the
-- substrate law puts in C: set-returning functions as table sources (one
-- lexical.senses() per token, one bubble_up per candidate relation type), relation-name
-- identifiers split with string_to_array per row, and an O(n^2) join of 277-315
-- candidate senses against each other through an OR of both directions that no
-- consensus index can serve. Rewriting it as two indexed joins behind a
-- MATERIALIZED fence still measured 82s.
--
-- The C form is the same computation as a MEMBERSHIP SCAN: candidates fetched
-- once, then one indexed range read per direction with an O(1) hash probe per
-- edge. consensus.relation_rank and the canonical name come from the manifest in C
-- (laplace_relation_lookup), and the name's object token becomes a content id
-- through the same hash the substrate uses everywhere -- so no per-row SQL
-- function call survives anywhere in the read.
--
-- Returns, per prompt token, its best sense and the signals it was chosen by:
--   specificity  coherence / own rated mass when connected; otherwise exact
--                inverse container frequency. These are alternative observed
--                signals, never an additively weighted blend.
--   coherence    rated mass to the OTHER tokens' candidate senses
--   rel_mass     rated mass in a relation type another token NAMES (the
--                "what are the X of Y" shape, where X is a relation not a peer)
--   total_mass   ALL rated mass on the candidate -- specificity's denominator,
--                exposed for the electors' inverse-mass fallback (below)
--
-- RANK ON SPECIFICITY, NEVER ON MASS. Every mass-shaped scalar tried here has
-- elected function words, because they are wired to everything: denote_mu picked
-- the article and TZAR, highway breadth tied "a" with "pawn", and raw coherence
-- put `is`/`of`/`was` first on every prompt measured. The share of a candidate's
-- own mass that reaches the rest of the prompt is scale-free and separates them
-- cleanly -- measured on "What is a pawn in chess?": total mass a = 4.28e16,
-- chess = 5.28e14, pawn = 2.63e13, and pawn/chess elect correctly.
--
-- THE SINGLE-CONTENT-WORD LIMIT (2026-08-01). A prompt with one content word
-- has no pair to cohere with: every candidate returns specificity 0 and the
-- election fell through to denote_mu, which favors function words -- "What is
-- a glacier?" elected the article (denote_mu 1169.7 vs 1082.3) and answered
-- about the letter A. total_mass (specificity's denominator, computed here all
-- along and discarded) is now a column; the INVERSE-mass election it was first
-- exposed for was REFUTED by measurement on the foundation-only seed (the
-- article's elected sense is LATIN SMALL LETTER A, 5.85e12 -- BELOW glacier,
-- dog and napoleon; the 4.28e16 article of the earlier notes was a UD-era
-- token, not a law), and mass DESC fails "parts of a car" (parts > car). The
-- The elector sites declared and pinned by ElectorArchitectureGateTests instead
-- break the all-silent case by ord DESC -- recency among sense-bearing candidates,
-- resolve_last_word's semantics restricted to tokens the graph holds senses for.
-- total_mass stays exposed: it is the signal that consensus.refuted the premise, and the
-- election diagnostic reads it.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace.prompt_coherence(text);
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION converse.prompt_coherence(p_prompt text)
    RETURNS TABLE(ord int, tok bytea, synset_id bytea,
                  coherence double precision, denote_mu numeric, peers bigint,
                  rel_type_id bytea, rel_mass double precision,
                  specificity double precision, total_mass double precision)
-- witnesses + lang_agree ARE computed and ARE the comparator's new sort keys
-- (src/prompt_coherence.c), but they are NOT declared here yet, deliberately.
--
-- laplace_substrate is in shared_preload_libraries, so the postmaster pins the
-- image and every backend inherits it by fork; an installed .so is inert until
-- PostgreSQL restarts. Widening this TABLE without that restart puts a 12-column
-- descriptor in front of a 10-column C function, and tuplestore_putvalues then
-- reads two Datums past the end of its stack arrays -- an overread on the live
-- converse path, observed 2026-08-05 returning NULLs for both columns.
--
-- The C symbol-integrity gate does NOT catch this: every symbol resolves. Symbol
-- existence is not signature agreement, and nothing in the sync path compares
-- returned column counts across the image boundary.
--
-- Re-add both columns in the same change that bounces PostgreSQL. Until then the
-- keys still rank -- they live in the comparator, not in the output.
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_prompt_coherence'
    LANGUAGE C STABLE;
